  "narrative": "**Narrative — Eicosanoid Dysregulation in the Treatment Group**\n\nThe RaMP enrichment analysis identifies **Eicosanoid Synthesis (WikiPathways WP167)** as the top candidate pathway (FDR = 0.0, fold-enrichment ≈ 1001), with five of the ten input metabolites — arachidonic acid (C00219), leukotriene A4 (C00909), 15-HETE (C04742), 5-HETE (C04805), and 15-deoxy-Δ12,14-PGJ2 (C14717) — mapping to it. A secondary high-confidence hit is the **Arachidonic Acid Metabolism** KEGG module (map00590), consistent with the WikiPathways result.\n\n**Key drivers.** Arachidonic acid (C00219) is the central hub: KEGG membership queries confirm it is annotated in the Arachidonic Acid Metabolism pathway (map00590), and the graph traversal confirms it is the obligate precursor. From it, the 5-lipoxygenase branch leads to leukotriene A4 (C00909), and the 12/15-lipoxygenase branch leads to 15-HETE (C04742). Both branches are active downstream of the hub (bidirectional/forward paths of length 2 confirmed via `query_kegg_path`). The cyclopentenone prostaglandin 15-deoxy-Δ12,14-PGJ2 (C14717) branches off the same arachidonate pool via the cyclooxygenase pathway.\n\n**Biological significance.** Coordinated elevation of arachidonate-derived lipid mediators points to treatment-induced activation of phospholipase A2, releasing membrane arachidonic acid, followed by parallel stimulation of 5-LOX, 12/15-LOX, and COX-2 branches. Leukotriene A4 is a potent chemoattractant for neutrophils; 15-HETE and 15-deoxy-PGJ2 are immunomodulatory eicosanoids with roles in resolving inflammation. The concurrent presence of 5-HETE (also a 5-LOX product) strengthens the case for widespread eicosanoid pathway activation. Copper (C00070), which co-enriched in the Selenium Micronutrient Network, may act as a cofactor for antioxidant enzymes that normally dampen eicosanoid-driven inflammation. Histamine (C00388) and gentisic acid (C00628) suggest ancillary oxidative-stress and phenolic-antioxidant responses. Dihydrothymine (C00906) is a pyrimidine oxidation product consistent with mild nucleobase damage downstream of the inflammatory burst. The overall signature is characteristic of acute inflammatory lipid mediator storm with concurrent oxidative-stress markers.\n\n**Verified upstream/downstream relationships:** Arachidonic acid (C00219) → Leukotriene A4 (C00909) via 5-HPETE (C05356); Arachidonic acid (C00219) → 15-HETE (C04742) via 15-HPETE (C05966) — both paths confirmed.",
